    <statement><p>Consider the surface <me>16 x^{2} + 4 y^{2} + 1 z^{2} = 21</me> and the point <m>P = \left( 1, 1, 1 \right)</m> on this surface.</p>
<p>A. Starting with the equation <m>x = 1 + 32 t</m>, find equations for
y and z which combine with this equation to give parametric equations for the
normal line through P.</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>z =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be expressions of t; e.g. <lq/>3x - 4y<rq/></p>
<p>B. Find an equation for the tangent plane through P.</p>
<p><m>z =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be expressions of x and y; e.g. "3xy + 2y"</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1+8t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1+2t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-16x-4y+21</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
